# Initial Setup's Range Finder page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigHWRangeFinder.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate binds the type combo to RNGFND_TYPE and starts the 200 ms timer that shows
# cs.sonarrange and cs.sonarvoltage (ConfigHWRangeFinder.cs:17-45); Deactivate stops it (:36-39).
#
# What SITL cannot exercise: the page's only write. SITL's copter numbers its rangefinders
# (RNGFND1_TYPE), and the C# binds RNGFND_TYPE, the name of firmware before 4.0 - so the combo
# stays disabled, as it does in Mission Planner against this firmware, and there is nothing to
# write and restore. The combo's write and the page's TeraRanger handler are covered by the unit
# tests in crates/mp-gui/src/config/rangefinder.rs. With no rangefinder SITL sends no RANGEFINDER,
# so the timer shows zeros: "0", the float's text, where the Designer's "0.0" stood.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-rangefinder.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 7
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.RNGFND1_TYPE 0

click tab-setup
expect config.rangefinder.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigHWRangeFinder
expect setup.page ConfigHWRangeFinder
expect config.rangefinder.active true
expect config.rangefinder.enabled true
expect config.rangefinder.heading RangeFinder

# RNGFND_TYPE is not SITL's: the combo is disabled, and nothing can be chosen from it.
expect config.rangefinder.type.enabled false
click rangefinder-RNGFND_TYPE
expect config.rangefinder.write none
expect params.value.RNGFND1_TYPE 0

# The timer has run in the two seconds settled.
expect config.rangefinder.timer true
expect config.rangefinder.readouts >= 5
expect config.rangefinder.distance 0
expect config.rangefinder.voltage 0
expect config.rangefinder.write none
expect config.rangefinder.message none

# Deactivate stops the timer.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
expect config.rangefinder.active false
expect config.rangefinder.timer false
